# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERSONAL DATA AND CREDENTIALS — the containing repository is PUBLIC.
#
# `following.json` is the user's Instagram social graph: 1,288 accounts, by handle, with the
# timestamp each was followed. The scan output derives from it and carries the bio, follower
# count and category of every one of them. Neither belongs in a public repository, and neither
# is needed there — the code reproduces the output from an export the user holds.
#
# A cookie is a live session credential. Committing one hands over the account.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/following.json
data/*.jsonl
data/report/
cookie.txt
*.cookie
.env

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
